<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine wholesale electricity prices cut 24 pct.</title>
<headline>Argentine wholesale electricity prices cut 24 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine wholesale electricity prices will be cut by 24 percent from November 1, the Energy Secretariat said Thursday.</p>
<p>Residential tariffs will be cut by five percent and industrial rates by seven percent from the same date.</p>
<p>The government decided to cut tariffs in its six-monthly review because of 1,200 MW extra generating capacity coming on line --- thanks to a new stage of the Yacyreta hydroelectric dam and new gas generators -- and also because of lower summer demand, a Secretariat spokesman said.</p>
<p>-- Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655</p>
</text>
